  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t03-q19",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation.t5",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A table showing students classified by gender and by result (pass/fail) is a:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "One-way (simple) table"
   },
   {
    "en": "Three-way table"
   },
   {
    "en": "Frequency curve"
   },
   {
    "en": "Two-way table"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Two characteristics (gender and result) are shown together: a two-way table."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t03-q20",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation.t5",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A college has 500 students, of whom 300 are boys. 240 boys and 160 girls passed. In a two-way table, the total number of students who failed is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "40"
   },
   {
    "en": "60"
   },
   {
    "en": "100"
   },
   {
    "en": "140"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Girls = 500 − 300 = 200. Boys failed = 300 − 240 = 60; girls failed = 200 − 160 = 40; total failed = 100."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t03-q21",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A class such as \"below 10\" or \"60 and above\" is called:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "A mid-value"
   },
   {
    "en": "An exclusive class"
   },
   {
    "en": "An open-end class"
   },
   {
    "en": "An inclusive class"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "An open-end class has its lower or upper limit missing."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t03-q22",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation.t5",
  "stem": {
   "en": "The part of a statistical table that tells where the data were taken from is the:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "Head note"
   },
   {
    "en": "Source note"
   },
   {
    "en": "Caption"
   },
   {
    "en": "Stub"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "The source note, below the table, names the origin of the data so readers can verify them."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t03-q23",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-03-classification-and-tabulation.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "The mid-values of a frequency distribution are 15, 25, 35 and 45. The class intervals are:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "15–25, 25–35, 35–45, 45–55"
   },
   {
    "en": "10–20, 20–30, 30–40, 40–50"
   },
   {
    "en": "10–15, 20–25, 30–35, 40–45"
   },
   {
    "en": "5–15, 15–25, 25–35, 35–45"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Width = difference of mid-values = 10. Each class runs from mid − 5 to mid + 5: 10–20, 20–30, 30–40, 40–50."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 }
]
